    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **22 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp13Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` field \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` (integer, min 0) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `Integer namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter. It's populated once at creation and mapped to the DTO automatically by MapStruct.\n\n3. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 In `saveOwner`, for a new owner I compute `namesakeCount` via a new `countNamesakes` helper (case-insensitive match on first + last name over `ownerRepository.findAll()`). Because it runs *before* the new owner is persisted \u2014 exactly like the existing `customerCode` logic \u2014 it counts only owners that existed before this create.\n\n4. **DB schemas/data** \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column to all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and appended the trailing value to the positional seed inserts in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` files (h2/postgres use column-list inserts, so no data change was needed).\n\nThe value is a snapshot fixed at creation time and persisted, so it's returned unchanged on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 matching the spec and the Cp13 test's expectation of `namesakeCount = 1` for the second same-named owner.",
